<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolt</p><h1 class="enc-title">Attack on the Moncada Barracks</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1953</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuban-revolution">Cuban Revolution</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The attack on the Moncada Barracks was an assault on an army post in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santiago">Santiago</a> de <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuba">Cuba</a> on 26 July 1953 by about 160 rebels led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fidel-castro">Fidel Castro</a>. It failed, and many captured rebels were killed; Castro was tried, gave his speech 'History Will Absolve Me' and was imprisoned until an amnesty in 1955. The date gave its name to his 26th of July Movement.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/attack-on-the-moncada-barracks.jpg" alt="Attack on the Moncada Barracks" width="320" height="244" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Moncadabarracks1953.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
